=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_4a7b — Weekday Dinner: Yuki Cooks at the Counter, Table Serves, Dog Eats on the Floor

Marco is out at his afternoon-to-night shift (home around 23:00), so Yuki runs the evening alone. The robot's 20:00 pass on day 0 captures the full dinner sequence: pan and spatula on the counter (active cooking), cutting board and knife at the sink (mid-wash), pot in the drawer (set aside), and the kitchen table loaded with Yuki's plate, glass, water bottle, and the serving dish. The dog food bag has moved from the pantry shelf to the kitchen floor, and the dog bowl is with it — the dog eats around 19:00–19:30 and the bag and bowl stay on the floor through the evening.

This document sets itself apart by modelling the 19:00–21:00 in-use window for the full set of cooking and dining objects simultaneously, rather than treating each object's resting spot in isolation. The existing documents place these objects at their storage locations (cupboard, drawer, pantry) for the entire 9–17h block and fall through to statistics outside it; none of them captures the coordinated shift to counter, sink, and table that the 20:00 pass shows.

Refutation: if the robot sees the pan, spatula, or cutting board back in the cupboard/drawer before 21:00 on a weekday, or sees the dog food bag still on the pantry shelf at 20:00, this document's dinner window is too wide or mis-timed.

