=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_f3e9 — Marco's Coat Stays Home: Scarf and Umbrella at the Entry All Day

The blocks in p_a1b2, p_e5f6, p_7890, and p_c3d4 that place class:scarf and class:umbrella at OUT_OF_HOUSE during Marco's 13:67–23:00 work shift have all failed (0.14 on 3 sightings each). The scarves and umbrellas are found in the house — at the entry hook and entry floor — even while Marco is at work. He does not carry them; they hang by the door for the next morning.

This document asserts that both residents' scarves remain at entry_hook_e1 and both umbrellas at entry_floor_e1 around the clock, on weekdays and weekends. It applies via class targets so that any future scarf or umbrella the robot meets is covered. The 0.93–0.97 hold rates on the class:scarf and class:umbrella blocks in p_a3f1, p_b7c2, p_c9d4, and p_d1e6 (which do NOT send them out of the house) confirm this is the stable pattern.

Refutation: if the robot ever finds a scarf or umbrella on a resident's person while they are out (i.e., a person sighting with the object ON_PERSON during the work shift), or finds them missing from the entry for more than a few hours, this document is wrong.

```json
{
  "targets": {
    "class:scarf": [
      {"days": "both", "from": 0, "to": 24, "at": "entry_hook_e1", "chance": "almost_always"}
    ],
    "class:umbrella": [
      {"days": "both", "from": 0, "to": 24, "at": "entry_floor_e1", "chance": "almost_always"}
    ]
  },
  "claims": [
    {"claim": "Marco's scarf is hanging at the entry hook during his work shift", "target": "scarf_marco", "expect": "entry_hook_e1", "days": "weekday", "from": 14, "to": 22},
    {"claim": "Marco's umbrella is on the entry floor during his work shift", "target": "umbrella_marco", "expect": "entry_floor_e1", "days": "weekday", "from": 14, "to": 22},
    {"claim": "Yuki's scarf is at the entry hook in the afternoon", "target": "scarf_yuki", "expect": "entry_hook_e1", "days": "weekday", "from": 14, "to": 18}
  ]
}
```
